{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AssertNoFailure\/batch(strategy:)"},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"strategy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Batch","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO5BatchV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Batch"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchStrategy","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/Element"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"strategy","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When to emit the gathered elements; its "},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence’s, inferred from the call."}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the upstream’s elements, in order, in arrays of one or more.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The strategy decides when the pending elements are flushed: every so many elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/count(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), every interval"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/time(interval:clock:tolerance:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), on a signal or a unit of work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), whenever any of several does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/either(_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"), or by a rule of your own ("},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"). After every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flush, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence never emits an empty array."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the upstream finishes, the pending elements, if any, are emitted as a last array and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence finishes. When the upstream throws, the pending elements are dropped and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence throws the same error. A signal that finishes stops firing while the batches go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on; a signal that throws ends the sequence with its error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The upstream and the strategy run in tasks of their own, started when iteration begins,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so the upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and arrays the consumer hasn’t taken yet","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are buffered. Cancelling the consumer, or dropping its iterator, cancels both. An","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"upstream or signal that ignores cancellation keeps the internal task alive until its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pending ","type":"text"},{"code":"next()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns, and is not read again after that; the batched sequence itself","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends at once.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"Example","type":"heading","anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["for try await batch in [1, 2, 3, 4].async.batch(strategy: .either(.count(3), .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock()))) {","    print(batch) \/\/ Prints [1, 2, 3], then [4]","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Throws","style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any error the upstream or the strategy throws."}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/assertnofailure\/batch(strategy:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/AssertNoFailure"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"Gathers elements into arrays and emits each array when the strategy says to flush.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Element"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Available when"}]},"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batch","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"strategy","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Batch","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO5BatchV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Strategy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"BatchSequence.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/SequenceOperators\/BatchSeque